From 0c1384de5edcfccbe72b5b11e49f51cd693e5046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: milliluk-erik <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:41:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 28/49] coco3: add -serial-out to capture bit-banger serial to

Originally coco3-only: the option was global, but only coco3.c consumed
it, so on a CoCo 1/2 -serial-out was accepted and captured nothing --
the same PIA1-A bit 1 bit-banger, silently ignored.  The config moves to
xroar.c/xroar.h as xroar_serial_out_file/_baud (it was always parsed
there; "coco3_" in the name was just where the first tap happened to
live), and the dragon family grows the identical tap: armed for the CoCo
family only, since the Dragons' serial is different hardware on
different lines -- there the option now warns loudly instead of arming.
The CoCo ROM print hook keeps its bit-bang shortcut only while the tap
is off, same rule as coco3_print_byte, so ROM output reaches the tap at
signal level too.
